Kernel build directories:

    GBA/      - GameBoy Advance console, plain build (mGBA / VBA-M / flash
                cartridge). Has no real disk: the root filesystem is a ROM
                memory disk embedded in the kernel image (device md0; root
                on md0a, swap on the md0b EWRAM region).  Run from an
                EverDrive, the root can be written and swap moves to the
                PSRAM after it (options MD_ROOT_RW, dev/md_gba.c).

    GBALOG/   - The GBA build plus AGBPrint console output to the
                emulator's log window (mGBA, VisualBoyAdvance).

    GBAED/    - GameBoy Advance with the EverDrive GBA X5 cartridge. Reads
                its root filesystem from the cartridge's real SD card
                (controller ed0, device sd0); root on /dev/sd0b (2nd MBR
                partition), crash dumps on /dev/sd0c (3rd).  Swaps to the
                EverDrive's PSRAM (md0b), so the EWRAM swap region becomes
                user RAM: a larger user window than the plain GBA build.
